---
description: Testing requirements
globs:
  - "src/**/*.py"
  - "tests/**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use pytest.
- Include nominal, boundary, invalid-input, and numerical-tolerance cases.
- Use pytest.approx for floating-point comparisons.
- For analytic Jacobians, compare against central finite differences.
- Test periodic identities where applicable.
- Tests must be deterministic unless explicitly testing randomized behavior.
- Randomized tests must use an explicit seed.
- Run the relevant test file after every implementation.
- Run the full test suite before declaring an issue complete.